      "id": "PM-18",
      "title": "Vendor Expediting, Factory Readiness & Incoterms Logistics",
      "desc": "Track shop drawings, sub-supplier components, DDP/DAP customs clearance, and laydown yard sequencing to site.",
      "tags": [
        "Expediting",
        "Incoterms",
        "Supply Chain"
      ],
      "folder": "Phase_3_Procurement_Contracts_RIBA_4\\PM-18_Vendor_Expediting_Incoterms_Logistics",
      "keyFacts": [
        "Incoterms 2020: EXW / FCA (Client transit risk) vs. CIF / DAP / DDP (Seller risk)",
        "Heavy Haulage: Dublin/Cork Ro-Ro -> police-escorted night low-loader for 63MVA Tx",
        "OEM Preservation: Space heaters ON, dry N2 purge, bi-weekly shaft rotation",
        "Expediting Triggers: Sub-tier PCB/breaker factory audits prior to FAT",
        "Receiving Check: Shock/tilt logger inspection (< 3g) before off-loading"
      ],
      "readme": "# PM-18: Vendor Expediting, Factory Readiness & Incoterms Logistics\n\n- **Phase**: `Phase 3: Procurement, Contracts & Supply Chain (RIBA 4)`\n- **RIBA Stage**: `RIBA Stage 4-5`\n- **P6 Milestone Gate**: `M3120 Customs/Port`\n- **WBS Scope**: `WBS 3.0-PROC`\n- **Governing Standards**: ICC Incoterms 2020 (EXW/FCA/CIF/DAP/DDP), Dublin/Cork Heavy Haul\n- **Focus Areas**: Breakers / PLC Sub-Supply, Marine Freight, Ro-Ro Abnormal Loads, Space Heaters / N2 Purge, OEM Custody\n\n## Module Overview\nTrack shop drawings, sub-supplier components, DDP/DAP customs clearance, and laydown yard sequencing to site.\n\n## Ordered Flashcard Documents (`Doc 1` -> `Doc 4`)\n\n| Doc | Category | Title | Exact Local File | Companion / Notes |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Doc 1 | Standard | ICC Incoterms 2020 Rules (EXW / FCA / CIF / DAP / DDP) & Expediting Guide | `PM18_Doc1_Standard_ICC_Incoterms_2020_Rules_EXW_FCA_Rev.004.docx` | ICC Incoterms 2020 |\n| Doc 2 | Deliverable | Weekly OEM Production, Sub-Supplier (Breakers/PLC) & Shop Drawing Tracker | `PM18_Doc2_Deliverable_Weekly_OEM_Production_Sub_Supplier_Rev.004.xlsx` | Tier-2 Component Tracking |\n| Doc 3 | Template | Marine Freight, EU Customs Clearance, Abnormal Load Route & Laydown Plan | `PM18_Doc3_Template_Marine_Freight_EU_Customs_Clearance_Rev.004.xlsx` | Dublin/Cork Heavy Haul |\n| Doc 4 | Audit | Delivered Equipment Preservation, Space-Heater Power & Nitrogen Purge Audit | `PM18_Doc4_Audit_Delivered_Equipment_Preservation_Rev.004.xlsx` | Storage Warranty Protection |\n\n## Study Takeaway (`Why Each Document Matters`)\n- **Doc 1 (Standard)**: Determine exact freight insurance, VAT customs liability, and site unloading boundaries.\n- **Doc 2 (Deliverable)**: Catch sub-tier PCB or breaker delays months before missed factory delivery dates.\n- **Doc 3 (Template)**: Coordinate Garda escorts, bridge weight limits, and crane pads for 100t transformers.\n- **Doc 4 (Audit)**: Protect switchgear insulation and chiller bearings during damp Irish winters on site.\n",
